# Topics

The main abstraction in Kafka. Topics are feeds of messages that producers write to and consumers read from.

---

# Partitions

Topics are divided into partitions for scalability and parallelism. Each partition is an ordered, immutable sequence of records.

---

# Records

Individual messages in Kafka. Each record consists of a key, a value, a timestamp, and optional headers.

---

# Consumers


Applications that read data from Kafka topics. Consumers can be organized into consumer groups for parallel processing.

---

# Offset

A unique sequential ID assigned to each record within a partition. Consumers use offsets to track their position in the log.

---

